ength":"strong","sentiment":"mixed","description":"Henry supplies the language and examples through which Dorian aestheticizes experience and consequence.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-3","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-sibyl","label":"Idealized lovers","strength":"strong","sentiment":"mixed","description":"Dorian loves Sibyl’s art, rejects the real woman, and lives under the consequence of her suicide.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-4","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-sibyl","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-james","label":"Protective siblings","strength":"strong","sentiment":"positive","description":"James’s love for Sibyl becomes the oath that pursues Prince Charming across eighteen years.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-5","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-sibyl","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-mrs-vane","label":"Daughter and theatrical mother","strength":"strong","sentiment":"mixed","description":"Mrs Vane depends on Sibyl’s career and hopes Dorian’s wealth will rescue the family.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-6","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-james","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-mrs-vane","label":"Son and mother divided by secrecy","strength":"medium","sentiment":"mixed","description":"James’s departure is darkened by the truth of his illegitimacy and his mother’s evasions.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-7","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-james","label":"Hunted man and avenger","strength":"strong","sentiment":"negative","description":"James seeks to kill Dorian for Sibyl’s death; Dorian’s unchanged face briefly defeats him.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-8","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-alan","label":"Former intimacy turned coercion","strength":"strong","sentiment":"negative","description":"Dorian uses a private secret to force Alan to destroy Basil’s remains.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-9","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-adrian","label":"Corrupting association","strength":"medium","sentiment":"negative","description":"Adrian’s ruin is publicly associated with Dorian’s hidden circle.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-10","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-victor","label":"Master and suspicious valet","strength":"medium","sentiment":"mixed","description":"Dorian controls Victor’s access after moving the portrait and fears observation.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-11","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-francis","label":"Master and servant","strength":"medium","sentiment":"neutral","description":"Francis serves Dorian through the murder aftermath, Selby panic, and final locked-room discovery.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-12","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-mrs-leaf","label":"Former charge and housekeeper","strength":"medium","sentiment":"positive","description":"Mrs Leaf remembers Dorian’s childhood and innocently gives him the schoolroom key.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-13","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-duchess","label":"Society flirtation","strength":"medium","sentiment":"positive","description":"The Duchess’s interest sustains Dorian’s public performance at Selby Royal.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-14","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-hetty","label":"Aborted seduction","strength":"medium","sentiment":"mixed","description":"Dorian spares Hetty but uses her heartbreak as evidence in a self-centred reform experiment.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-15","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-henry","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-basil","label":"Old friends and philosophical rivals","strength":"medium","sentiment":"mixed","description":"Basil resists Henry’s influence while Henry treats Basil’s moral seriousness as material for paradox.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-16","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-henry","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-victoria","label":"Detached marriage","strength":"medium","sentiment":"neutral","description":"Their marriage is socially polished but emotionally remote.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-17","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-henry","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-agatha","label":"Nephew and aunt","strength":"medium","sentiment":"positive","description":"Lady Agatha hosts Henry despite his habit of mocking philanthropy and convention.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-18","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-henry","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-fermor","label":"Nephew and worldly uncle","strength":"medium","sentiment":"positive","description":"Lord Fermor supplies Henry with Dorian’s family history.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-19","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-kelso","label":"Grandson and violent guardian","strength":"medium","sentiment":"negative","description":"Dorian inherits wealth from the grandfather suspected of arranging his father’s death.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-20","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-dorian","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-margaret","label":"Son and idealized dead mother","strength":"strong","sentiment":"positive","description":"Dorian’s beauty and romantic ancestry are repeatedly linked to Margaret Devereux.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-21","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-sibyl","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-isaacs","label":"Actress and creditor-manager","strength":"medium","sentiment":"negative","description":"Isaacs employs Sibyl and uses the Vane family’s debt to maintain control.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-relationship-22","characterAId":"dorian-gray-char-duchess","characterBId":"dorian-gray-char-geoffrey","label":"Siblings","strength":"medium","sentiment":"positive","description":"The Duchess and Geoffrey attend Dorian’s Selby gathering together.","isBidirectional":true,"startEventId":null}],"relationshipSnapshots":[],"timelines":[{"id":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","worldId":"dorian-gray-world","name":"The Picture of Dorian Gray — Master Chronology","description":"One reading-order timeline for the expanded twenty-chapter novel; flashbacks and the long Chapter XI passage retain explicit calendar positions.","color":"#74566c","dayOffset":0,"createdAt":1785528000000}],"chapters":[{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-01","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":1,"title":"Chapter I","synopsis":"Basil Hallward’s studio and his guarded account of Dorian establish the triangle of artist, sitter, and influencer.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-02","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":2,"title":"Chapter II","synopsis":"Lord Henry awakens Dorian’s terror of aging; Dorian’s wish binds his fate to Basil’s completed portrait.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-03","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":3,"title":"Chapter III","synopsis":"Lord Henry learns Dorian’s violent family history, then enthralls him at Lady Agatha’s luncheon.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-04","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":4,"title":"Chapter IV","synopsis":"Dorian tells Lord Henry that he has fallen in love with the actress Sibyl Vane and announces their engagement.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-05","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":5,"title":"Chapter V","synopsis":"Sibyl’s family prepares for James’s departure; he vows to kill Prince Charming if Dorian harms her.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-06","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":6,"title":"Chapter VI","synopsis":"Basil and Lord Henry debate Dorian’s engagement before Dorian takes them to judge Sibyl’s art.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-07","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":7,"title":"Chapter VII","synopsis":"Sibyl acts badly because real love has displaced theatrical illusion; Dorian rejects her and the portrait changes.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-08","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":8,"title":"Chapter VIII","synopsis":"Dorian tries to repent, learns of Sibyl’s death, and lets Lord Henry convert tragedy into aesthetic experience.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-09","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":9,"title":"Chapter IX","synopsis":"Basil comes to mourn Sibyl, confesses what the portrait meant to him, and unknowingly gives Dorian reason to hide it.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-10","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":10,"title":"Chapter X","synopsis":"Dorian moves the portrait into his locked schoolroom and begins the long education of the yellow book.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-11","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":11,"title":"Chapter XI","synopsis":"Nearly eighteen years pass as Dorian pursues sensations, collections, and secret vice while society remains divided about him.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-12","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":12,"title":"Chapter XII","synopsis":"On the eve of Dorian’s thirty-eighth birthday, Basil confronts him about years of ruinous rumours.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-13","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":13,"title":"Chapter XIII","synopsis":"Dorian reveals the portrait, then murders Basil when the painter urges prayer and repentance.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-14","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":14,"title":"Chapter XIV","synopsis":"Dorian blackmails Alan Campbell into using chemistry to destroy Basil’s body and burns the remaining evidence.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-15","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":15,"title":"Chapter XV","synopsis":"Dorian performs normality at Lady Narborough’s dinner, then seeks oblivion in an opium den.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-16","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":16,"title":"Chapter XVI","synopsis":"In the opium den, a woman names Dorian “Prince Charming,” allowing James Vane to find and nearly kill him.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-17","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":17,"title":"Chapter XVII","synopsis":"At Selby Royal, Dorian’s society performance collapses when he sees James Vane watching through the conservatory window.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-18","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":18,"title":"Chapter XVIII","synopsis":"Dorian’s fear follows him into the shooting party until Geoffrey accidentally kills the concealed James Vane.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-19","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":19,"title":"Chapter XIX","synopsis":"Dorian claims that sparing Hetty Merton proves reform, but Lord Henry exposes the vanity beneath the gesture.","notes":"","wordGoal":null},{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-chapter-20","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","number":20,"title":"Chapter XX","synopsis":"Dorian finds hypocrisy recorded on the portrait and destroys the canvas, restoring it while revealing his own true body.","notes":"","wordGoal":null}],"events":[{"worldId":"dorian-gray-world","createdAt":1785528000000,"updatedAt":1785528000000,"id":"dorian-gray-event-1","chapterId":"dorian-gray-chapter-01","timelineId":"dorian-gray-timeline-main","title":"Basil First Sees Dorian","description":"At Lady Brandon’s crowded reception, Basil is overwhelmed by the sight of Do